label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-05","finding":"Safety Requirements for Active Play Equipment - Used According to Manufacturer's Instructions: It was determined during the investigation that the operation did not have manufacturing instructions for the kinder aged playground located at the operation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026610720","violation_type_title":"Safety Requirements for Active Play Equipment - Used According to Manufacturer's Instructions (26 TAC §746.4601(2))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260225-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2507-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260225","date":"2026-02-25","original_code":"746.2507(4)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-04-13","finding":"Activities for Toddlers - Provide Large Muscle Development: It was determined during the investigation that the victim was playing on equipment that is not age appropriate for a twenty-three-month-old. The playground equipment was designed for older children and presented an injury risk to the victim.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026610723","violation_type_title":"Activities for Toddlers - Provide Large Muscle Development (26 TAC §746.2507(4))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260225-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1203-3-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260225","date":"2026-02-25","original_code":"746.1203(3)(A)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-04-13","finding":"Administrative and clerical duties that take caregiver's attention away from children: It was determined during the investigation that the caregiver used her cell phone to complete an incident report while still on the playground with the children present. The caregiver was alone with eight children and completion of the incident report took her attention away from the children she was responsible for.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026610721","violation_type_title":"Administrative and clerical duties that take caregiver's attention away from children (26 TAC §746.1203(3)(A))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260225-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260225","date":"2026-02-25","original_code":"746.1205(a)(5)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-04-13","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Intervene to ensure each child's safety: It was determined during the investigation that the caregiver did not intervene to provide the victim with first aid treatment. The victim's eye was injured. Ice or other medical aid was not provided to the victim. The caregiver took the child back to the classroom after the injury on the playground and did not notify her immediate supervisor or another caregiver that the victim needed first aid for their injured eye, nor did the caregiver attempt to provided first aid themselves for the victim. The victim remained in the classroom injured until the parent picked up without first aid being provided.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026610719","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Intervene to ensure each child's safety (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(5))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495832-i20260203","date":"2026-02-03","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905887074","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905887074","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2026-02-03","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurr